# Strumming: Offbeat Chops (repertoire plan: st-strum-reggae). An original 16-bar study on two
# small chords on strings 4, 3 and 2: Am (xx755x) and D (xx777x), two bars each, all the way through.
# Fingers: Am, finger 3 on string 4 fret 7 and finger 1 flat across strings 3 and 2 at fret 5;
# D, lay finger 3 flat across all three strings at fret 7 (or use fingers 2, 3 and 4). Finger 3
# never leaves string 4, fret 7. The fretting fingers also rest lightly against strings 5 and 1
# so that only the three middle strings sound.
# Bars 1-8: a chop on the "and" of every beat, played as an up-strum while the hand keeps moving
# down-up and the downs miss the strings. Bars 9-16: the half-time feel, a down-strum chop on beats
# 2 and 4 only, with a pickup chop on the "and" of 4 in bar 12. Every chop is cut short at once by
# easing the fretting fingers off the frets (they stay touching the strings), so the beat itself is
# silent. The teacher's bass plays on the beats underneath. With D major over A, the colour is the
# Dorian F#; the key is written as A minor.
title: Strumming: Offbeat Chops
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original strumming study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: strumming, offbeat, reggae, ska, muting
tempo: 80
time: 4/4
key: Am

track: Your chops
role: rhythm
[Every and]
strum: -U-U-U-U
| "Am=xx755x" ^"chop on every and" e r U r U r U r U | % | "D=xx777x" e r U r U r U r U | % |
| "Am=xx755x" e r U r U r U r U | % | "D=xx777x" e r U r U r U r U | % |
[Half-time: 2 and 4]
strum: --D---D-
| "Am=xx755x" ^"chop on 2 and 4" q r e D r q r e D r | % | "D=xx777x" q r e D r q r e D r | q r e D r q r e D U |
| "Am=xx755x" q r e D r q r e D r | % | "D=xx777x" q r e D r q r e D r | % ||

